  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe chord-sag allowance moved out of `cross_entry.rs` into a new `operation/cross_sag.rs`, which now welds vertices before matching edges. A non-conforming STL round whose facets share no vertices gets the same allowance as a welded one, so the cross-hole mouth and the #84 shank reach read the true surface, not the chords.\n\n- Weld tolerance: 1e-6 × the model's bounding diagonal, with a floor of 1e-9 mm. The only importer weld tolerance is the user's `RepairModel` parameter, so there's no default to reuse.\n- Spatial hash: cells the size of the tolerance, a 27-cell lookup, and the earliest vertex in input order wins. It's O(n), deterministic and saturating, so nothing can panic. Edges that collapse to one point are skipped.\n- The dihedral and width rules are unchanged; a larger allowance only moves the entry outward, into air.\n\n## Pins\n\n- `operation::cross_entry::tests::an_unwelded_round_is_entered_and_reached_as_the_welded_one`: entry and reach match the welded mesh within 1e-9 and sit at or outside the true surface. **Fails on main**: 4.283 unwelded against 4.948 welded.\n- `operation::cross_sag::tests::an_unwelded_round_edge_carries_the_allowance_and_an_open_edge_none`: the unwelded half fails on main; a real open edge still gets 0.\n\n## Readings\n\napp lib 68; drill_reach 6, drill_reach_fit 3, drilling_cross 9, _box 7, _part 3, _rapids 2, _spindle 6, _stock 8, lathe_cross_drill 4; clippy on app is clean.\n\nChangelog: Cross-hole entry and shank reach read a non-conforming (unwelded) STL round at its true surface, not its chords\n\nFixes #121\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
